  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Akbar Husain vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 7 February, 2024 Author: Prem Narayan Singh Bench: Prem Narayan Singh 1 In The High Court Of Madhya Pradesh At Indore Crr No. 539 of 2024 (Akbar Husain And Others Vs The State Of Madhya P Dated : 07-02-2024 Shri Akhilesh Kumar Saxena, learned counsel for the peti Shri H.S. Rathore, learned Government Ad respondent/State. Heard on I.A. No. 2299/2024, which is an application filed under Section 389 of the Code of Criminal Procedure, 1973 on behalf of appellants for suspension of sentence and grant of bail.",
    "facts": "2. The appellants have been convicted for offence under Section 3(zz), 26(2)(ii) read with Section 51 & 59(i) of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 and sentenced to undergo 6-6 months R.I., with fine of Rs.10,000/- and usual default stipulation.",
    "arguments": "3 . Learned counsel for the appellant submits that the appellants are innocent and have been falsely implicated in the matter. He further submitted that final hearing of this appeal is likely to take sufficient long time."
  },
